In <23sfhjINNpdg@sheoak.ucnv.edu.au> ashlin@ironbark.ucnv.edu.au (Vance Ashlin) writes:

>I've heard a lot about Nethack having '--' versions '++' versions, etc.
>What I want to know is the following:

>   - What is the latest Nethack

	NetHack 3.1.3 (Version 3.1, patchlevel 3)

>   - Is it available in DOS binary executable format?

	Yes.  The official release is available in two versions for DOS:  
	nh313pc.exe (uses overlays, runs on 286 or better with 1 M or
	better of memory, min. 540k of conventional) and nh313386.exe 
	(protected mode, requires 386 or better with lots of memory, no 
	overlays).

>     - if so at what anonymous FTP site

	The official release is available by anonymous FTP from the NetHack
	official site:  linc.cis.upenn.edu.  For PC binaries, cd to
	pub/NH3.1/binaries/PC after FTP'ing to linc, then get the files.  
	It will also be on lots of other sites, such as wuarchive.wust.edu.

>   - what is the difference between the '--' and '++' versions (if any)?

	Neither of these is official NetHack.  They are modified to add
	monsters and stuff that some hacker though was cute.  Originally
	this hacked version of NetHack was called NetHack++, but C++ purists
	objected to use of ++ for a non-C++ program, as misleading, so
	the authors changed the name to NetHack--.

